**Assignment Title** Studio 1.1 Assignment 1.1
**Prompt** Create an abstract composition that explores line, shape, and contrast. Use a mixture of straight, curved, thick, and thin lines. Include geometric shapes such as circles, triangles, and squares, along with a few organic shapes. Use strong contrast by placing black shapes and lines against a white background, with a few bright red shapes to attract attention. Arrange the shapes asymmetrically so the composition feels active and interesting. Make one large red circle the focal point. Use the differences in line direction, shape size, and color to create visual variety while keeping the composition unified.
**Vocabluary** Form: 
In both the artwork there are various shapes such as circles,rectangles,triangles and squares. Curved lines also are used adding geometric variety and making it interesting 

Volume: in both artworks the variety of small shapes add a sense of volume while the big red circles are highlighted the most and take up the most space.

Mass: the mass of the bold and  red and black shapes look much heavier as they mark more visual weight while the other shapes showcase less visual weight 

Texture: in both the artworks most of the surface appear to be smooth and flat. The curved and thin lines also add a lot of texture. Also in the second artwork the Gray shaded area contribute a lot to adding texture. 

Conclusion: both the artworks use bold color shapes and lines to show the mass volume shape and texture efficiently. The large red circles make an eye catching visual to look at. Overall all these factors makes the artworks look visually appealing and interesting

