**Assignment Tile** Studio 1.1 Assignment 2.2
**Prompt** Create an abstract three-dimensional composition that explores form, volume, mass, and texture. Include solid forms such as spheres, cubes, and cylinders. Make the objects appear to have volume by using highlights, shadows, and changes in value. Show mass by making some objects look heavy, solid, and substantial. Include a variety of textures, such as rough stone, smooth glass, and bumpy surfaces. Arrange the objects at different distances to create depth and use lighting to make their forms appear realistic. Keep the background simple so the forms, volume, mass, and textures are easy to observe.
**Vocabluary** Form: these artworks use 3D shapes which create a realistic look. The shapes used are spheres cubes cylinders and rectangles.

Volume: due to the 3D shapes the object are appeared to take up real space. The large sphere cube and cylinder are close and creates more sense of volume 

Mass: 
The stone cubes and heavy blocks look really heavy. The dark shadows give them a visual weight. And they also look solid which makes the viewer assume there mass to be heavy.

Texture:
There is not only one texture highlighted in these artworks. There are various textures like the glass sphere and cube are smooth while the wooden sphere have a woody grainy texture and the metal sphere has a bumpy texture. Because of the variety of textures the artwork and objects look more realistic 

Conclusion: 
The use of 3D geometric shapes,shadows and variety of textures give these composition a very realistic visual. The arrangementof objects also plays a huge rule in making it appear more interesting

